6357258 1089 "q-98344" 13194139535605 true] [17592186357258 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535605 true] [17592186357258 1100 "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(-3,-1,-2)=1, &  & {f}_{x}(-3,-1,-2)=4, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(-3,-1,-2)=-3, &  & {f}_{z}(-3,-1,-2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-3,-1,-2)$ estimate the value of $f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03).$" 13194139535605 true] [17592186357258 1113 #uuid "e291dc27-d17d-5da1-907a-8c20b4b06f0a" 13194139535605 true] [17592186357258 1145 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-3,-1,-2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(-3,-1,-2)+∇f(-3,-1,-2)\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩ \\\\  & =f(-3,-1,-2) \\\\  & \\,+⟨{f}_{x}(-3,-1,-2),{f}_{y}(-3,-1,-2),{f}_{z}(-3,-1,-2)⟩\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=-3.04,$ $y=-1.02,$ and $z=-2.03$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03) & ≈1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3.04+3,-1.02+1,-2.03+2⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.04,-0.02,-0.03⟩ \\\\  & =1-0.16+0.06+0.06 \\\\  & =0.96\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357260 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357261 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357262 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357263 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357264 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1041 "selection" 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357260 13194139535605 true] [17592186357259 1110 #uuid "830a98bf-d229-53db-9248-dcecf3b8e9e6" 13194139535605 true] [1759218